DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ssttrrccaasseeccmmpp() and ssttrrnnccaasseeccmmpp() functions compare the null-terminated
     strings _s_1 and _s_2.

     The ssttrrnnccaasseeccmmpp() function compares at most _l_e_n characters.  The
     ssttrrccaasseeccmmpp__ll() and ssttrrnnccaasseeccmmpp__ll() functions do the same as their non-lo‐
     cale versions above, but take an explicit locale rather than using the
     current locale.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The functions ssttrrccaasseeccmmpp() and ssttrrnnccaasseeccmmpp() return an integer greater
     than, equal to, or less than 0, depending on whether _s_1 is lexicographi‐
     cally greater than, equal to, or less than _s_2 after translation of each
     corresponding character to lower-case.  The strings themselves are not
     modified.  The comparison is done using unsigned characters, so that
     ‘\200’ is greater than ‘\0’.  The functions ssttrrccaasseeccmmpp__ll() and
     ssttrrnnccaasseeccmmpp__ll() do the same but take explicit locales.

